## Prerequisites

| Tool              | Version                        | Notes                                 |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |
| **Git**           | ≥ 2.40                         | clone & version control               |
| **Node.js**       | see `.nvmrc` / `.node-version` | use a version manager (`nvm`, `asdf`) |
| **pnpm**          | ≥ 9.0                          | enable via `corepack enable`          |
| Docker (optional) | _latest_                       | run the app in a container            |

```bash
# one‑off with nvm
a) nvm install       # installs the version from .nvmrc
b) nvm use           # switches your shell to that version
```

---

## Getting Started

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/your‑org/spark.git
cd spark

# 2. Switch to the correct Node version (if you haven’t already)
nvm use   # or `asdf install && asdf shell nodejs $(cat .tool-versions)`

# 3. Install dependencies
pnpm install

# 4. Run the development server
pnpm start
```

The app boots on **[http://localhost:8888](http://localhost:8888)** by default. Runtime configuration is loaded from an `.env` file—copy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust as necessary.

---

## Common pnpm Scripts

| Command        | Description                                                    |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `pnpm start`   | Transpiles (if needed) & starts the app in watch mode          |
| `pnpm build`   | Creates an optimized production build in `dist/`               |
| `pnpm test`    | Runs Jest unit tests with coverage                             |
| `pnpm lint`    | Runs ESLint & Prettier checks                                  |
| `pnpm release` | Generates a semantic release (tags, changelog, GitHub release) |

---

## Husky Git Hooks

The `.husky/` directory contains Git hooks installed automatically after `pnpm install`.

| Hook         | What it runs                               | Purpose                                                              |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `pre-commit` | `pnpm lint && pnpm test --passWithNoTests` | Prevents style & test regressions from landing in `main`.            |
| `commit-msg` | `commitlint --edit $1`                     | Rejects commit messages that do not follow **Conventional Commits**. |

> **Why Husky?** Re‑usable, project‑level hooks make it impossible to “forget” local checks and keep the CI pipeline green.

